diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e6e795d..18103a2 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,13 +9,33 @@ persistence is an in-memory repository behind a small interface.
   append-only `Ledger`; never stored. Only receipts, adjustments (counts,
   write-offs) and shipments write to the ledger.
 - **Allocated** — units promised to `PLACED` orders that have not shipped yet.
-- **Available** — `on_hand - allocated`, floored at zero. This is what new
-  orders may take.
+- **Held** — units held by `ACTIVE` reservations that have not expired.
+- **Available** — `on_hand - allocated - held`, floored at zero. This is what
+  new orders and reservations may take.
 
 Order lifecycle: `place_order` (allocates, all lines or nothing) →
 `ship_order` (writes `SHIPMENT` ledger entries) or `cancel_order` (releases
 the allocation).
 
+Reservation lifecycle (checkout holds stock before payment): `reserve` →
+`confirm_reservation` (becomes a `PLACED` order; the hold turns into its
+allocation) or `release_reservation`. A hold nobody confirms lapses 20 minutes
+after creation (`RESERVATION_TTL`); expiry is evaluated lazily against the
+clock, so there is no sweep job. Holds never touch the ledger.
+
+- `reserve` holds as much of each line as is available, up to the amount asked;
+  lines with nothing available are dropped. It fails with `InsufficientStock`
+  only if nothing at all can be held.
+- Idempotency keys are global and bound forever to the first successful
+  request. Repeating the same request (same warehouse and requested items)
+  returns the original reservation in whatever state it is now; a different
+  request under the same key raises `IdempotencyConflict`. A failed `reserve`
+  leaves no trace.
+- Confirming twice returns the same order. Confirming an expired hold raises
+  `ReservationExpired`; a released one, `InvalidReservationState`.
+- Releasing a released or expired hold is a no-op; releasing a confirmed one
+  raises `InvalidReservationState` (cancel the order instead).
+
 ## Conventions
 
 - All time comes from an injected `Clock` (`FixedClock` in tests). Never call
